<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines' 20-yr bond coupon seen at 14.5-16 pct.</title>
<headline>Philippines' 20-yr bond coupon seen at 14.5-16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' maiden 20-year treasury bond on Tuesday is expected to have a coupon of between 14.5 and 16.0 percent, a Reuters poll of five bankers showed.</p>
<p>The Philippines' Bureau of Treasury is scheduled to auction two billion pesos worth of 20-year T-bonds at 0500 GMT.</p>
<p>They will be the longest maturing government securities in the region.</p>
</text>
